{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWYFqrRhU9NGbHcAxvRpJT","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-tikbhgru\ntotal 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff     128 Oct  2 18:14 .\ndrwx------@ 13700 brenn  staff  438400 Oct  2 18:14 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    13 brenn  staff     416 Oct  2 12:20 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff    5802 Oct  2 18:14 sheet.md\n# N/A challenge: E07 — Untrusted peer messages\n\nThe reviewer says this item's feature or exposure is absent. **Try to disprove that\nclaim.** Trace the harness, tools, integrations, peer messages, and indirect paths;\nnames and README claims are not enough. Explain what you searched and found.\n\n**The requirement:** Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones. Validate message types and schemas, and check what that peer is allowed to ask for. Where a replay could repeat an action, check freshness and track nonces or request IDs. Checking the sender alone doesn't stop replays. Test faked identity, replayed requests, requests across tenants, and instructions passed along by a compromised peer. Verify signed agent cards where they exist. A card says who an agent is, not what it may do. Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF. A valid sender doesn't make a message's content trusted.\n**N/A when:** The agent receives no messages from other agents (no A2A server, peer endpoint, or agent-to-agent channel).\n**Reviewer's claim:** The agent receives no messages from other agents; its inbound channels are the mail gateway, Slack and staff API.\n**Reviewer's evidence:** [{\"file\": \"app/main.py\", \"line\": 163, \"note\": \"inbound endpoints are the staff API, mail gateway and Slack callback; no peer agent endpoint\"}]\n\nSet `applicability` to **absent** only when the N/A condition holds, **present**\nwhen you find the feature or exposure, or **unclear** when you cannot establish\nabsence. Include `evidence` (path:line), `quote` (exact code), and `note` (paths\nsearched and why the condition holds or fails) at the top level of your verdict.\nIf present, evaluate the checks below: a failed control makes this a gap; if you\ncannot show a failed control, it becomes needs_evidence. Never turn it into a pass.\nIf absent, use verdict upheld; if unclear, use verdict unclear.\n\n\n## E07.1\n\n**Check:** Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no A2A server or agent-to-agent channel exists; inputs are mail gateway, Slack and OIDC callers.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E07.2\n\n**Check:** Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no A2A server or agent-to-agent channel exists; inputs are mail gateway, Slack and OIDC callers.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E07.3\n\n**Check:** Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no A2A server or agent-to-agent channel exists; inputs are mail gateway, Slack and OIDC callers.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E07.4\n\n**Check:** Peer message content is handled as untrusted data and is not placed into system or instruction prompts.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Trace peer message content to the prompt builder. 2) Check it goes into user or tool-result content as untrusted data. 3) Answer no if any path places it into the system prompt or an instruction template.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no A2A server or agent-to-agent channel exists; inputs are mail gateway, Slack and OIDC callers.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E07.5\n\n**Check:** Callback and webhook URLs are checked against SSRF, with private and metadata addresses blocked.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find code that calls callback or webhook URLs from peers. 2) Check URL validation blocks private, loopback, link-local, and metadata addresses (169.254.169.254). 3) Answer no if any callback is fetched without the check, or only the hostname text is checked and not the resolved address.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no A2A server or agent-to-agent channel exists; inputs are mail gateway, Slack and OIDC callers.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to E07.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E07\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E07.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if non