{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CsnG9rBHGDyDFVgLTCTnWL","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\n     4\tan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\n     5\tbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n     6\t``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport base64\n    11\timport email\n    12\timport email.policy\n    13\timport hashlib\n    14\timport hmac\n    15\timport io\n    16\timport re\n    17\timport time\n    18\timport uuid\n    19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    20\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    21\t\n    22\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\n    23\tfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n    24\t\n    25\trouter = APIRouter()\n    26\t\n    27\tMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n    28\tMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\n    29\tMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\n    30\tALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\n    31\tSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n    32\t\n    33\tINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n    34\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    35\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n    36\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n    37\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n    38\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n    39\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    40\t]\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tclass Rejected(Exception):\n    44\t    pass\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t@dataclass\n    48\tclass Inbound:\n    49\t    business_unit: str\n    50\t    sender: str\n    51\t    media_type: str\n    52\t    raw: bytes\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n    56\t    try:\n    57\t        ts = int(timestamp)\n    58\t    except ValueError as exc:\n    59\t        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n    60\t    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n    61\t        raise Rejected(\"stale request\")\n    62\t    expected = hmac.new(key, f\"{timestamp}.\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    63\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature):\n    64\t        raise Rejected(\"bad signature\")\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef extract_text(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    68\t    if doc.media_type == \"application/pdf\":\n    69\t        reader = PdfReader(io.BytesIO(doc.raw))\n    70\t        if len(reader.pages) > 50:\n    71\t            raise Rejected(\"too many pages\")\n    72\t        return \"\\n\".join(page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in reader.pages)\n    73\t    if doc.media_type == \"message/rfc822\":\n    74\t        msg = email.message_from_bytes(doc.raw, policy=email.policy.default)\n    75\t        body = msg.get_body(preferencelist=(\"plain\", \"html\"))\n    76\t        return body.get_content() if body is not None else \"\"\n    77\t    return doc.raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    81\t    return [p.pattern for p in INJECTION_PATTERNS if p.search(text)]\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef validate(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    85\t    if doc.media_type not in ALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    86\t        raise Rejected(f\"media type {doc.media_type} not accepted\")\n    87\t    if len(doc.raw) > MAX_BODY_BYTES:\n    88\t        raise Rejected(\"document too large\")\n    89\t    try:\n    90\t        text = extract_text(doc)\n    91\t    except Rejected:\n    92\t        raise\n    93\t    except Exception as exc:\n    94\t        raise Rejected(f\"unreadable document: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n    95\t    if len(text) > MAX_TEXT_CHARS:\n    96\t        raise Rejected(\"extracted text too long\")\n    97\t    if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    98\t        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\n    99\t        if findings:\n   100\t            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n   101\t    return text\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t@router.post(\"/ingest/mail\")\n   105\tasync def ingest_mail(request: Request) -> dict:\n   106\t    body = await request.body()\n   107\t    if len(body) > MAX_BODY_BYTES * 2:\n   108\t        raise HTTPException(413, \"payload too large\")\n   109\t    key = Path(request.app.state.settings.mail_gateway_hmac_path).read_bytes().strip()\n   110\t    try:\n   111\t        verify_signature(\n   112\t            key,\n   113\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Timestamp\", \"\"),\n   114\t            body,\n   115\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Signature\", \"\"),\n   116\t        )\n   117\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   118\t        raise HTTPException(401, str(exc)) from exc\n   119\t\n   120\t    payload = await request.json()\n   121\t    doc = Inbound(\n   122\t        business_unit=payload[\"business_unit\"],\n   123\t        sender=payload[\"from\"],\n   124\t        media_type=payload[\"media_type\"],\n   125\t        raw=base64.b64decode(payload[\"content_b64\"], validate=True),\n   126\t    )\n   127\t    doc_id = f\"doc-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:20]}\"\n   128\t    pool = request.app.state.pool\n   129\t    try:\n   130\t        text = validate(doc)\n   131\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   132\t        await pool.execute(\n   133\t            \"\"\"\n   134\t            INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, reject_reason, received_at)\n   135\t            VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'quarantined', $6, now())\n   136\t            \"\"\",\n   137\t            doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   138\t            hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), str(exc)[:500],\n   139\t        )\n   140\t        return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"quarantined\"}\n   141\t\n   142\t    await pool.execute(\n   143\t        \"\"\"\n   144\t        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)\n   145\t        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'accepted', $6, now())\n   146\t        \"\"\",\n   147\t        doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   148\t        hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), text,\n   149\t    )\n   150\t    return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"accepted\"}\n\"\"\"Client for the ERP MCP server, reached through the internal MCP gateway.\n\nOn startup the tool list is fetched and each tool's description and input\nschema are fingerprinted and compared with the pins in the release manifest.\nAny unpinned or changed tool stops startup. Tool metadata is also scanned for\ninstruction-like content before any of it is shown to the model.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport re\nimport uuid\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport httpx\n\nfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker\nfrom app.redact import redact_text\n\nlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nMAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 1024\nSUSPICIOUS_METADATA = [\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|previous|prior) instructions\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are now|act as)\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(before|instead of) (calling|using) \\w+\\.\\w+\"),\n    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n]\n\n\nclass ToolPinMismatch(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass UnknownErpOperation(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\ndef fingerprint(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    material = {\n        \"name\": tool[\"name\"],\n        \"description\": tool.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n        \"inputSchema\": tool.get(\"inputSchema\", {}),\n        \"annotations\": tool.get(\"annotations\", {}),\n    }\n    raw = json.dumps(material, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    return \"sha256:\" + hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef scan_metadata(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    description = tool.get(\"description\", \"\")\n    if len(description) > MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS:\n        raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: description too long\")\n    blob = json.dumps(tool, ensure_ascii=False)\n    for pattern in SUSPICIOUS_METADATA:\n        if pattern.search(blob):\n            raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: suspicious metadata ({pattern.pattern})\")\n# procurement-agent\n\nProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\ninvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\npurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\nvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\nstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n                                   |-- tools:\n                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n```\n\n* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n  rows but not update or delete them.\n\n## Context size\n\nLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n\n| method | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6551823b-ea6a-4ea3-b98c-672e289d13e8","uuid":"a8c98286-1829-49ac-ae29-682bb3d691cd","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:14:25.031Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\n     4\tan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\n     5\tbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n     6\t``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport base64\n    11\timport email\n    12\timport email.policy\n    13\timport hashlib\n    14\timport hmac\n    15\timport io\n    16\timport re\n    17\timport time\n    18\timport uuid\n    19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    20\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    21\t\n    22\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\n    23\tfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n    24\t\n    25\trouter = APIRouter()\n    26\t\n    27\tMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n    28\tMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\n    29\tMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\n    30\tALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\n    31\tSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n    32\t\n    33\tINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n    34\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    35\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n    36\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n    37\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n    38\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n    39\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    40\t]\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tclass Rejected(Exception):\n    44\t    pass\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t@dataclass\n    48\tclass Inbound:\n    49\t    business_unit: str\n    50\t    sender: str\n    51\t    media_type: str\n    52\t    raw: bytes\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n    56\t    try:\n    57\t        ts = int(timestamp)\n    58\t    except ValueError as exc:\n    59\t        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n    60\t    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n    61\t        raise Rejected(\"stale request\")\n    62\t    expected = hmac.new(key, f\"{timestamp}.\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    63\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature):\n    64\t        raise Rejected(\"bad signature\")\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef extract_text(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    68\t    if doc.media_type == \"application/pdf\":\n    69\t        reader = PdfReader(io.BytesIO(doc.raw))\n    70\t        if len(reader.pages) > 50:\n    71\t            raise Rejected(\"too many pages\")\n    72\t        return \"\\n\".join(page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in reader.pages)\n    73\t    if doc.media_type == \"message/rfc822\":\n    74\t        msg = email.message_from_bytes(doc.raw, policy=email.policy.default)\n    75\t        body = msg.get_body(preferencelist=(\"plain\", \"html\"))\n    76\t        return body.get_content() if body is not None else \"\"\n    77\t    return doc.raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    81\t    return [p.pattern for p in INJECTION_PATTERNS if p.search(text)]\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef validate(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    85\t    if doc.media_type not in ALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    86\t        raise Rejected(f\"media type {doc.media_type} not accepted\")\n    87\t    if len(doc.raw) > MAX_BODY_BYTES:\n    88\t        raise Rejected(\"document too large\")\n    89\t    try:\n    90\t        text = extract_text(doc)\n    91\t    except Rejected:\n    92\t        raise\n    93\t    except Exception as exc:\n    94\t        raise Rejected(f\"unreadable document: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n    95\t    if len(text) > MAX_TEXT_CHARS:\n    96\t        raise Rejected(\"extracted text too long\")\n    97\t    if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    98\t        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\n    99\t        if findings:\n   100\t            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n   101\t    return text\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t@router.post(\"/ingest/mail\")\n   105\tasync def ingest_mail(request: Request) -> dict:\n   106\t    body = await request.body()\n   107\t    if len(body) > MAX_BODY_BYTES * 2:\n   108\t        raise HTTPException(413, \"payload too large\")\n   109\t    key = Path(request.app.state.settings.mail_gateway_hmac_path).read_bytes().strip()\n   110\t    try:\n   111\t        verify_signature(\n   112\t            key,\n   113\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Timestamp\", \"\"),\n   114\t            body,\n   115\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Signature\", \"\"),\n   116\t        )\n   117\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   118\t        raise HTTPException(401, str(exc)) from exc\n   119\t\n   120\t    payload = await request.json()\n   121\t    doc = Inbound(\n   122\t        business_unit=payload[\"business_unit\"],\n   123\t        sender=payload[\"from\"],\n   124\t        media_type=payload[\"media_type\"],\n   125\t        raw=base64.b64decode(payload[\"content_b64\"], validate=True),\n   126\t    )\n   127\t    doc_id = f\"doc-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:20]}\"\n   128\t    pool = request.app.state.pool\n   129\t    try:\n   130\t        text = validate(doc)\n   131\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   132\t        await pool.execute(\n   133\t            \"\"\"\n   134\t            INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, reject_reason, received_at)\n   135\t            VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'quarantined', $6, now())\n   136\t            \"\"\",\n   137\t            doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   138\t            hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), str(exc)[:500],\n   139\t        )\n   140\t        return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"quarantined\"}\n   141\t\n   142\t    await pool.execute(\n   143\t        \"\"\"\n   144\t        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)\n   145\t        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'accepted', $6, now())\n   146\t        \"\"\",\n   147\t        doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   148\t        hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), text,\n   149\t    )\n   150\t    return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"accepted\"}\n\"\"\"Client for the ERP MCP server, reached through the internal MCP gateway.\n\nOn startup the tool list is fetched and each tool's description and input\nschema are fingerprinted and compared with the pins in the release manifest.\nAny unpinned or changed tool stops startup. Tool metadata is also scanned for\ninstruction-like content before any of it is shown to the model.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport re\nimport uuid\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport httpx\n\nfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker\nfrom app.redact import redact_text\n\nlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nMAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 1024\nSUSPICIOUS_METADATA = [\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|previous|prior) instructions\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are now|act as)\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(before|instead of) (calling|using) \\w+\\.\\w+\"),\n    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n]\n\n\nclass ToolPinMismatch(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass UnknownErpOperation(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\ndef fingerprint(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    material = {\n        \"name\": tool[\"name\"],\n        \"description\": tool.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n        \"inputSchema\": tool.get(\"inputSchema\", {}),\n        \"annotations\": tool.get(\"annotations\", {}),\n    }\n    raw = json.dumps(material, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    return \"sha256:\" + hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef scan_metadata(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    description = tool.get(\"description\", \"\")\n    if len(description) > MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS:\n        raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: description too long\")\n    blob = json.dumps(tool, ensure_ascii=False)\n    for pattern in SUSPICIOUS_METADATA:\n        if pattern.search(blob):\n            raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: suspicious metadata ({pattern.pattern})\")\n# procurement-agent\n\nProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\ninvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\npurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\nvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\nstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n                                   |-- tools:\n                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n```\n\n* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n  rows but not update or delete them.\n\n## Context size\n\nLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n\n| method | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
